.TH SSHD 8
.SH NAME
sshd \- the SSH server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /bin/sshd
(started by
.BR init (8))
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sshd
listens on TCP port 22. It is in init's table, started at boot if
.B /etc/ssh/sshd_config
exists; otherwise it ends at once and is not started again. It is off by
default; to turn it on, as root:
.PP
.nf
mkdir /etc/ssh
echo on > /etc/ssh/sshd_config
svc restart sshd
.fi
.PP
On its first start it makes its host key and logs its fingerprint:
.BR "sshd: listening on port 22, host key SHA256:..." .
.PP
Passwords are checked by the accounts server,
.BR auth (8)
.RB ( AUTH_CHECK ),
which then starts the user's shell
.RB ( AUTH_LOGIN ,
with the password again, which opens an encrypted home). Keys are read
from
.B ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
(OpenSSH's format,
.B ssh-ed25519
lines); a locked encrypted home's keys cannot be read. Root may log in
only with a key; 6 tries per connection; 2 minutes to log in.
.PP
sshd is to the remote shell what the console server is to the local
one: each connection slot (8) has a port,
.B sshd0
to
.BR sshd7 ;
the shell's terminal is
.BI sshd N # session\fR,
with the same line editing as the console.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/ssh/sshd_config
its switch (nothing in it is read yet).
.TP
.BR /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key ", " .pub
the host key (mode 0600).
.TP
.B ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
the keys that may log in.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR auth (8),
.BR svc (8),
.BR netd (4)
.SH BUGS
One channel per connection: no port forwarding, agent, X11, scp or sftp.
Ed25519 keys only; no
.B authorized_keys
options and no
.B sshd_config
settings. The remote terminal is 80 x 24 whatever the window. A session
ended by a signal reports status 255.
